- For every development request, start by writing a clear Gherkin feature file
- Reuse existing step definitions whenever possible before creating new ones
- Automate the scenario import and configure the BDD runner (e.g. `bdd_widget_test` for Flutter and `godog` for Go)
- Implement the step definitions for each Given/When/Then clause
- Confirm the BDD test fails initially (Red)
- Write only the minimal implementation to make the BDD test pass (Green)
- Refactor production code and step definitions without breaking any tests (Refactor)
- For each unit of business logic, apply TDD:
  - Write the unit test in Dart first and verify it fails
  - Implement just enough code to make the unit test succeed
  - Refactor both production code and tests as needed, keeping all tests green
- At the end of each development cycle, run linter and fix all reported issues before delivery (`flutter analyze` for Flutter and `golangci-lint` for Go)
